2. Theory
Alpha-Beta Pruning is an optimization technique used in Artificial Intelligence to improve the Minimax algorithm.

It is used in two-player games like Chess and Tic-Tac-Toe.

It works with two values:
- Alpha (α): Best value that the maximizing player can guarantee.
- Beta (β): Best value that the minimizing player can guarantee.
When Beta becomes less than or equal to Alpha (β ≤ α), further searching of that branch is stopped because it cannot affect the final decision.

This reduces unnecessary calculations and makes the search faster without changing the optimal result.

1. Chess: Helps AI select the best possible move.
2. Checkers: Evaluates possible moves and opponent responses.
3. Tic-Tac-Toe: Helps AI select optimal moves.
4. Connect Four: Evaluates winning and losing positions.
5. Othello/Reversi: Helps select strong moves.
6. Strategy Games: Reduces unnecessary game-tree calculations.
